    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the SGD 26.83 charged on TRP-00113 stands and no refund is due. The rider's claim is not supported by the evidence.\n\nWhy the distance argument does not succeed. This was a RYDE_POOL booking. Under POL-RD-12 the comparison baseline for a pooled trip is the matched pooled itinerary recorded on the trip record — trip_record.optimal_distance_km = 19.4 km, the platform's Punggol -> Hougang co-rider pickup -> Raffles Place route quoted at match time 18:42 — and not the rider's own solo optimal. The rider's 15.8 km figure is trip_record.solo_optimal_distance_km, which the policy carries for reference only, so the '28% longer' comparison is measured against the wrong field. Against the correct baseline, the distance actually driven — gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 20.18 km on EV-GPS-00113, the governing field under POL-RD-01 — exceeds 19.4 km by 0.78 km, which is 4.02%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is BOTH greater than 0.8 km absolute AND greater than 20% of optimal. 0.78 km fails the first test, and the trip record's rounded 20.2 km gives 0.80 km, still not greater than 0.8 because the test is strict; 4.02% fails the second by a wide margin. Both advocates reach this result. No deviation is established, so POL-RD-02's recomputation (which would have produced a 26.83 - 25.67 = 1.16, rounded up to 1.20, figure) never runs, and the SGD 26.83 billed for the pooled itinerary stands.\n\nWhy the Hougang leg is not a driver detour. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00113) shows the platform messaging the rider at 18:42:04, before the 18:47:10 start, that a co-rider had been matched and that the pooled route now included one Hougang Central pickup, quoted at 19.4 km and 34 minutes — the same 19.4 km stored as the matched-itinerary optimal. POL-RD-12 excludes co-rider collection distance on a platform-matched pool from any excess, and the driver drove the route the app displayed.\n\nOther points considered. The GPS trace is intact — 217 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, 10-second sampling against 10 seconds expected — so nothing is impaired under POL-RD-07 and no escalation arises under POL-RD-10(3). The traffic-advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is empty (a missing artifact at weight 0.0); neither side relies on it for exoneration and it affects nothing. No repeat-deviation pattern exists under POL-RD-06: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 471, so both tests fail, no uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arise. The fare carries no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge lines, so there is no billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4). All three instruments carry the same trip identifier TRP-00113 and consistent timestamps. POL-GEN-03 makes the outcome NO_ACTION on this rider-filed dispute: fare_breakdown.payment_status remains CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd remains 0.00. The finding rests on the trip record and the GPS trace, each at weight 1.0, so confidence is not discounted and stands at 0.95, above the 0.70 floor."
